         <description><![CDATA[<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/6e823b8d-6724-44c2-822e-3a29c32a54f4,1794315798798/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%281336%2C882%2C5862%2C3297%29%3B' alt='A men&apos;s basketball player is shown talking to a teammate at left, while a referee and opposing player are shown at right.' width='620' height='349' title='Zach Edey (14) of the Memphis Grizzlies is shown during the first half of a NBA game against the Toronto Raptors at Scotiabank Arena on Monday in Toronto.'/><p>Zach Edey had eight points and nine rebounds as his Memphis Grizzlies topped the Toronto Raptors 118-102 on Monday. It was only the the seven-foot-four centre's second time playing at the Raptors' home arena after he missed the Grizzlies' one game in Toronto last season due to injury.</p>]]></description>
